over and over again, don't touch that hot stove, it's good that they walk away with that memory. with that piece of information. So that's normal human psychology. That's actually quite adaptive. But when the information is wrong, and especially in these complicated information ecosystems, our echo chambers online or our kind of biased exposure to our friend groups, that kind of exposure can really solidify even wrong information.

16
