00:12:06.000 --> 00:12:46.000
of those kinds of claims. And so it's actually quite laborious to unearth some of these misconceptions. We say it like it's easy, but it takes a lot of work. And when people are busy, sometimes that's work that they don't have the bandwidth to pursue. Are some people more prone to believe these types of myths than others? For instance, did you find differences by gender or grade point average or other factors? Yeah. So our students reported their grade point average, which of course that could be incorrect. But let's just assume over all of these students, if there is an error in the reporting of their grade point average, they're all just slightly inflating.

