real consequences to holding misconceptions. We're going to take a short break. When we return, I'll talk with Dr. Smith about some of the real-world consequences. of these myths and misconceptions. Well, speaking of consequences, I mean, let's talk about why does this really matter. I mean, if people think that you only use 10% of your brain or that sugar makes children hyper, so what? And on one level, I commiserate with that conclusion because there do seem to be some misbeliefs where we can just say, all right, Uncle Johnny just believes something crazy.

