00:20:44.000 --> 00:21:27.000
It can mean a lot of different things. But one of the things that memory research shows is that when we self-generate memory links, they're more likely to stick. And so thinking about how do we engage students in the debunking process so that they are not just receiving from on high, this is not a true statement, in which case they might not actually remember it that way, but that they reasoned through that process of how did we arrive at this conclusion and what do you infer from what these data show? and then really helping them generate some of these conclusions on their own. I will say there's a member on our team who's also doing some really interesting work with having

